      "message": "Hi Yuxin,\n\nThanks for looking at this! My thoughts are\n\n1. This is probably caused by a call to FaceService#addLockoutResetCallback() along with the API callback coming from the actual sensor.\n\n```\n// After a quick search, this seems to be the only call that is not put on the handler thread (FaceService#addLockoutResetCallback())\n          mLockoutResetDispatcher.addCallback(callback, opPackageName);\n```\n\n2. If 1 is true, the best fix is probably to ensure FaceService#addLockoutResetCallback() is on the same handler as everything else, and we would probably submit this in our dev branch and let it trickle down to AOSP.\n\n\nAlso what further confirms my suspicion is that I see logs on your bugreport that sysui dies right before this modification, which would lead to them causing this. \n\nThis bug should be very infrequent, but does happen\n\n10-27 16:34:14.039  1000  2507  7243 I ActivityManager: Process com.android.systemui (pid 23295) has died: cch+85 SVC \n\nI\u0027ll speak with other folks on my team about this on Monday",
